WEBVTT

00:11.170 --> 00:13.100
Outing...

00:13.500 --> 00:15.730
Can't we go on one?

00:16.000 --> 00:18.370
Let's go, max outing!

00:18.570 --> 00:22.980
Outing, outing, outing right now!

00:23.080 --> 00:25.950
What are you doing?
Intensify your barrage!

00:26.410 --> 00:27.380
Hey!

00:35.260 --> 00:37.050
Shut the hell up...

00:38.990 --> 00:40.890
Huh? Uh... wha?

00:43.330 --> 00:48.230
Genshiken 2

01:07.260 --> 01:10.820
Our company assists
with self-publishing...

01:10.960 --> 01:14.950
...so our editors are more
concerned with collecting manuscripts...

01:15.060 --> 01:18.260
...scheduling, and budget
management than with planning.

01:19.030 --> 01:21.940
Do you feel you have
an aptitude for that?

01:22.170 --> 01:27.200
I have no accounting experience,
but I feel I'm positive and a hard worker.

01:27.680 --> 01:32.110
Also, we'd need you
to work for us at least one year.

01:32.210 --> 01:36.050
Your trial period is more than just your first
three months.

01:36.150 --> 01:40.990
It costs a lot of time and money to mold
a new employee into a usable shape.

01:41.390 --> 01:43.650
I realize that.

01:44.360 --> 01:46.550
That concludes the interview.

01:46.660 --> 01:48.460
Thank you very much.

01:49.960 --> 01:51.520
Thank you very much!

01:55.240 --> 01:58.140
Shinransha

01:58.470 --> 02:00.070
Another rejection...

02:00.180 --> 02:01.300
Damn it.

02:03.380 --> 02:04.640
Editor...

02:06.450 --> 02:09.350
So why'd I want to be one again?

02:09.350 --> 02:11.320
Magazoon

02:11.890 --> 02:14.450
Because it's a job
dealing with stuff I like?

02:14.560 --> 02:17.120
But then what about
anime and games?

02:19.730 --> 02:23.130
Either way, I lack
the ability to create them.

02:24.400 --> 02:26.920
I guess I've got to work
behind the scenes...

02:27.040 --> 02:30.490
...and manga has the smallest
number of such people involved.

02:31.170 --> 02:33.500
Was that my process of elimination?

02:34.210 --> 02:37.770
I said I wanted to use
my dojinshi experience and tried...

02:37.880 --> 02:41.750
...to appeal as the ordinary,
cheerful, optimistic otaku.

02:41.850 --> 02:45.510
But there were tons of
other guys doing the same thing.

02:49.390 --> 02:52.850
I've said that stuff
so many times in interviews...

02:52.960 --> 02:57.090
...it's even starting to seem like
a blatant lie to me at this point.

02:57.770 --> 02:59.600
What's the problem here?

02:59.700 --> 03:02.100
Is it me? Is it myself?

03:02.200 --> 03:03.860
The Society for the Study
of Modern Visual Culture

03:03.970 --> 03:06.000
Circle Enrollment Guide

03:15.320 --> 03:18.150
If only I hadn't joined
Genshiken, I'd be...

03:21.860 --> 03:23.820
Hey now, cut that out.

03:23.930 --> 03:26.890
All right, you got it. I'll teach you.

03:27.060 --> 03:29.120
Cinema

03:36.570 --> 03:38.540
Right, as if.

03:43.950 --> 03:45.880
In regards to your application...

03:45.980 --> 03:48.280
...but we regret to inform you that...

03:52.590 --> 03:54.990
Kodansha

04:01.100 --> 04:04.530
Okay, let's have a look
at your story concept.

04:04.830 --> 04:06.300
Y-Yes, sir.

04:13.880 --> 04:19.110
I'll get right to the point.
Did you want to draw this?

04:20.180 --> 04:23.580
Is this what you want to draw?
What you want to do?

04:24.550 --> 04:27.720
It really doesn't look that way to me.

04:28.390 --> 04:32.220
It feels... I don't know...
superficial or off the mark.

04:32.960 --> 04:38.870
Maybe you should give some deep
thought to what you truly want to draw.

04:40.070 --> 04:45.340
O-O-Okay, then what
is it you w-want to do?

04:45.570 --> 04:48.670
I'm surprised you can
say that to another person.

05:15.440 --> 05:18.300
I haven't even talked to Ogiue at all.

05:20.580 --> 05:21.510
Daiedo Trust Construction

05:21.510 --> 05:23.010
Daiedo Trust Construction
What do you think of PR?

05:23.010 --> 05:23.340
What do you think of PR?

05:23.440 --> 05:24.570
Yes, sir!

05:24.680 --> 05:28.550
Even if a product is excellent,
as long as the public isn't informed...

05:28.650 --> 05:31.810
...customers can't be
aware of how good it is.

05:32.220 --> 05:36.750
I want to do a job where
I can convey quality to people!

05:39.690 --> 05:43.760
I've only ever seen
distribution centers around here.

05:45.300 --> 05:48.790
Why is it you haven't
settled on a job at this point?

05:49.240 --> 05:51.300
Time must be running short.

05:51.410 --> 05:53.370
Yes, that's true.

05:54.280 --> 05:56.210
What field did you really want?

05:56.310 --> 05:58.300
I want to work here, sir.

05:58.410 --> 06:01.180
It's okay. Tell me the truth.

06:01.850 --> 06:02.840
Publishing.

06:03.250 --> 06:05.480
Aha, you don't say.

06:06.590 --> 06:09.850
So you wouldn't mind being in,
say, the accounting department?

06:09.960 --> 06:13.120
We don't currently need
anyone new in production.

06:14.360 --> 06:16.850
I-I'd be willing to do that.

06:22.240 --> 06:25.870
If you're gonna reject me,
don't take so long doing it!

06:29.010 --> 06:31.040
Jobhunt. Net

06:31.150 --> 06:35.340
It's almost all for programmers.
Why do they need so many?

06:37.120 --> 06:40.490
Retail, restaurants, service...

06:41.660 --> 06:44.560
That'd be great if I were Kasukabe.

06:45.130 --> 06:47.220
Technical stuff's out too.

06:49.430 --> 06:54.370
Maybe I'm not cut out for interviews,
or even job hunting at all?

07:06.480 --> 07:08.010
Hey, guys.

07:11.250 --> 07:13.380
What happened, Sasahara?

07:14.560 --> 07:16.610
A change of pace, I guess?

07:16.720 --> 07:19.220
It's kind of... unexpected.

07:20.090 --> 07:23.330
Yeah? I thought
it worked surprisingly well.

07:23.670 --> 07:27.100
Hey, listen. What say
we really plan an outing?

07:28.400 --> 07:31.700
We haven't all been
together in a while...

07:31.810 --> 07:35.300
...and if it's one night, maybe
even those working could make it.

07:35.680 --> 07:39.370
Wouldn't it be cheaper and less
crowded now than during summer?

07:39.480 --> 07:43.010
Uh, well... Outing... outing...

07:43.890 --> 07:47.510
Sorry for the other day.
I was kind of stressing a bit.

07:49.220 --> 07:52.450
How can you have
so much spare time every day?

07:52.560 --> 07:54.430
Are you really working?

07:54.960 --> 07:58.990
Do you really think
I'm that incompetent?

07:59.430 --> 08:00.530
Yeah.

08:01.300 --> 08:02.270
A beard?

08:02.370 --> 08:06.030
What's the story?
Have you gone rogue, Sasahara?

08:06.140 --> 08:08.440
Uh, no, not really...

08:08.740 --> 08:11.210
I don't know what to say.

08:11.950 --> 08:14.440
What, did you find a job?

08:14.550 --> 08:15.640
No.

08:16.550 --> 08:20.850
Well, I figured I might
just go without one for now.

08:22.520 --> 08:24.820
This year's history anyway.

08:24.930 --> 08:26.590
So next year!

08:26.690 --> 08:29.890
Now how about that outing, guys?

08:30.300 --> 08:34.530
Maybe you could say
I drowned in the rough seas of life.

08:35.040 --> 08:37.500
I guess I'm a loser.

08:38.270 --> 08:43.440
But at least now I know where
I stand in the grand scheme of things.

08:44.780 --> 08:47.840
Say what? You're just running away.

08:48.620 --> 08:49.810
S-Saki...

08:50.490 --> 08:55.320
No, Kasukabe's
got it right. You know?

08:57.020 --> 08:59.890
Self-derision, self-torture,
and self-justification?

08:59.990 --> 09:04.620
Otaku sure do love to say
with pride, "Hi, I'm a loser."

09:04.870 --> 09:07.300
Whoa... Whoa whoa whoa...

09:07.640 --> 09:12.230
N-Now who am I to talk when I didn't
get a job until after New Year's?

09:12.340 --> 09:15.900
But lots of things in life
are beyond our control.

09:16.280 --> 09:19.740
I know quite well how
hard this is for Sasahara.

09:19.850 --> 09:24.510
At the same time, I know
Kasukabe's rants are out of kindness.

09:25.590 --> 09:29.610
I knew you were lazy,
Sasayan, but I'm still disappointed.

09:37.130 --> 09:39.570
Well, hey...

09:41.500 --> 09:45.100
I thought you'd make it
in publishing, Sasahara.

09:48.510 --> 09:51.710
I understand why
Kasukabe feels disappointed.

09:55.180 --> 09:57.410
You're just running away.

09:57.520 --> 09:59.990
Self-derision, self-torture,
and self-justification?

10:00.090 --> 10:04.420
Otaku sure do love to say
with pride, "Hi, I'm a loser."

10:04.960 --> 10:08.450
I knew you were lazy,
Sasayan, but I'm still disappointed.

10:08.560 --> 10:12.020
But lots of things in life
are beyond our control.

10:12.130 --> 10:15.590
I know quite well how
hard this is for Sasahara.

10:15.700 --> 10:20.160
At the same time, I know
Kasukabe's rants are out of kindness.

10:20.270 --> 10:23.840
I thought you'd make it
in publishing, Sasahara.

10:27.620 --> 10:29.580
Kugayama

10:31.850 --> 10:34.220
Hi. It's been a while.

10:34.320 --> 10:38.350
I h-heard some b-blonde
characters showed up?

10:38.760 --> 10:40.160
Oh, that's right.

10:40.260 --> 10:44.790
I was thinking of asking you if it's
okay to show Irohagokko to them.

10:45.300 --> 10:46.660
S-Sure.

10:46.770 --> 10:48.390
Oh, really?

10:48.970 --> 10:55.070
Well, I'm j-just thankful there are
people out there who w-want to see it.

11:02.680 --> 11:05.380
Are you at a station
this late? That sucks.

11:05.690 --> 11:09.020
Y-Yeah. I'm getting by at least.

11:09.120 --> 11:12.790
I d-didn't pick
this j-job because I like it.

11:14.330 --> 11:16.350
Well, I'll g-get going.

11:16.460 --> 11:18.160
Uh, Kugayama!

11:21.170 --> 11:24.870
Did Madarame
or somebody ask you to call me?

11:25.040 --> 11:26.100
N-No.

11:26.970 --> 11:28.070
Oh...

11:28.580 --> 11:33.040
B-But hey, I'm, uh,
drawing a little again.

11:33.510 --> 11:36.970
It s-sure was fun, making a dojinshi.

11:37.790 --> 11:40.450
I c-can say that now anyway.

11:41.290 --> 11:42.650
S-See ya.

11:47.630 --> 11:50.870
Kuchiki

11:50.870 --> 11:51.200
Kugayama

11:51.200 --> 11:51.530
Kasukabe

11:51.530 --> 11:53.570
Ogiue

11:53.570 --> 11:56.470
Directory
Sasahara

12:21.860 --> 12:23.760
Manga Editor Wanted

12:34.140 --> 12:35.710
First interview. Interviewer,
Washidasha Editorial Production's
President. Satoru Kaneko

12:35.710 --> 12:38.250
First interview. Interviewer,
Washidasha Editorial Production's
President. Satoru Kaneko
Um...

12:38.250 --> 12:39.210
Passed

12:39.210 --> 12:39.680
Second interview. Interviewer,
Aforementioned Company's Employee.
Ryuuji Onodera

12:39.680 --> 12:43.810
Second interview. Interviewer,
Aforementioned Company's Employee.
Ryuuji Onodera
Yeah, you'll pass our first interview
unless something's really wrong.

12:44.250 --> 12:46.010
We're not in publication.

12:46.120 --> 12:50.720
We have contracts with various
publishers and send them editors.

12:50.830 --> 12:54.820
You could say we're a temp
agency that specializes in editors.

12:55.100 --> 12:58.900
We want people we can use in
the field, so someone in the field...

12:59.000 --> 13:01.200
...makes the final hiring decisions.

13:01.300 --> 13:04.240
You could say
the president is just for show.

13:06.640 --> 13:08.230
I kid, of course.

13:08.340 --> 13:11.400
So you're graduating
this year, Mr. Sasahara?

13:11.510 --> 13:12.210
Yes, sir.

13:12.210 --> 13:13.610
Yes, sir.
The usual ambition and motivation
bit is a waste of time, so we'll skip it.

13:13.610 --> 13:16.850
The usual ambition and motivation
bit is a waste of time, so we'll skip it.

13:16.950 --> 13:19.390
This guy's a little strange too.

13:19.450 --> 13:24.980
Your college circle is the "Society for
the... Study of Modern Visual Culture."

13:25.090 --> 13:28.080
Is that something like a manga club?

13:28.200 --> 13:32.330
There's really nothing wrong
with that interpretation...

13:32.430 --> 13:35.100
...but we study anime
and games as well.

13:35.670 --> 13:39.700
You don't say. So what did
you do within that framework?

13:40.510 --> 13:44.540
I served as chairman during my junior year...

13:44.650 --> 13:50.210
...and I assembled manuscripts and
published club bulletins and dojinshi.

13:50.450 --> 13:53.250
Dojinshi. Did you sell at Comic Fest?

13:53.350 --> 13:54.580
Yes, sir.

13:54.790 --> 13:56.420
Were they adult?

13:56.520 --> 13:57.720
Yes, sir.

13:57.830 --> 13:59.690
And you don't draw?

13:59.760 --> 14:02.250
Correct. I can't draw.

14:03.030 --> 14:04.830
Not at all?

14:05.500 --> 14:07.330
You've never tried?

14:07.440 --> 14:09.730
Well, when I was little...

14:09.840 --> 14:14.870
I guess I tried...
drawing something manga-ish...

14:14.980 --> 14:17.240
...but I wasn't any good at it.

14:18.850 --> 14:21.840
What do you think
of people who can draw?

14:23.350 --> 14:26.510
I've worked with
two artists in my circle.

14:27.620 --> 14:29.280
One is diligent...

14:29.590 --> 14:32.990
...and very easy to work with,
delivering with little prompting.

14:33.090 --> 14:35.890
The other has
the skill and the drive...

14:36.000 --> 14:39.060
...but has trouble taking
that one crucial step forward.

14:40.000 --> 14:44.300
But getting to work with
such artists was a lot of fun.

14:45.010 --> 14:46.130
Fun?

14:46.770 --> 14:49.300
It wasn't all fun of course.

14:49.410 --> 14:55.280
There was some trouble between us,
and it taught me my own limits.

14:56.450 --> 15:01.410
There I was, usually
the poster boy for easygoing guys...

15:01.520 --> 15:04.390
...getting into
a heated, volatile debate.

15:04.990 --> 15:08.090
I think the creation of
a dojinshi made that possible.

15:08.200 --> 15:10.490
Even with all
the heartache in account...

15:10.600 --> 15:13.330
...I can still say with
confidence that it was fun.

15:15.570 --> 15:16.700
I'm sorry.

15:16.800 --> 15:19.900
You asked what I think
about people who can draw...

15:20.010 --> 15:22.500
...and I ended up talking about myself.

15:22.610 --> 15:24.080
No, that's fine.

15:24.880 --> 15:28.340
This next question
is going to be extremely direct.

15:29.420 --> 15:33.280
What do you think is the worst
thing an editor can ever do?

15:34.390 --> 15:38.190
I think it's to make an artist
lose his or her motivation.

15:40.760 --> 15:42.290
Was that wrong?

15:42.530 --> 15:43.930
Not really.

15:44.030 --> 15:46.830
It's up there. I'm just the opposite.

15:48.470 --> 15:51.670
So on a different note,
what manga do you like?

15:54.240 --> 15:58.110
If I had to pick one,
I guess it'd be Kujibiki Unbalance.

15:58.210 --> 15:59.740
Ah, that one!

15:59.850 --> 16:03.580
Well, I was all about the president,
so in the anime and manga...

16:03.720 --> 16:07.950
...when she left the story,
it was like it was over for me.

16:10.320 --> 16:12.920
I happen to be in charge of that title.

16:13.430 --> 16:15.190
S-S-S-Seriously?

16:15.960 --> 16:18.860
I'm in the Magazoon
editorial department.

16:19.430 --> 16:22.200
T-Then I shouldn't have said that...

16:23.970 --> 16:28.770
Uh, you caught me off guard,
sizing me up all of a sudden like that...

16:28.880 --> 16:33.810
Like I said, we get sent to lots
of different editorial departments.

16:33.910 --> 16:36.180
We cover plenty of big names.

16:43.090 --> 16:44.990
Kanji Sasahara
Washidasha

16:45.790 --> 16:47.160
It's thick...

16:50.970 --> 16:51.200
Kohsaka

16:51.200 --> 16:51.700
Madarame

16:51.700 --> 16:52.030
Tanaka

16:52.030 --> 16:52.370
Kuchiki

16:52.370 --> 16:52.700
Kugayama

16:52.700 --> 16:53.030
Kasukabe

16:53.030 --> 16:53.860
Ogiue (Home)

16:55.800 --> 16:57.100
Here goes.

17:12.320 --> 17:16.020
Did I reach your place,
Ogiue? This is Sasahara.

17:16.120 --> 17:17.850
Is this a good time?

17:17.960 --> 17:19.190
Sure.

17:19.290 --> 17:24.290
Well, uh, I got a job.
I wanted to tell you.

17:25.800 --> 17:27.460
Congratulations.

17:27.570 --> 17:30.540
I owe you a lot of thanks.

17:30.740 --> 17:32.830
I mean...

17:32.940 --> 17:38.040
...well, what you and Kasukabe said
made me want to give it another try.

17:38.150 --> 17:41.080
Also, Kugayama
called and talked to me...

17:42.780 --> 17:47.520
Sorry, didn't mean to get too
personal. I just wanted to fill you in.

17:48.020 --> 17:50.120
No, it's not that.

17:50.560 --> 17:52.960
I-I was in the shower.

17:53.960 --> 17:54.890
Sorry!

17:55.000 --> 17:56.460
No, it's okay.

17:57.060 --> 18:00.520
Well, I really
mean it... thanks. See ya.

18:00.630 --> 18:01.620
Hey!

18:03.470 --> 18:07.930
I have a, um, story idea
I want you to see.

18:08.040 --> 18:09.870
Story idea? Me?

18:10.480 --> 18:12.600
It's okay if you can't.

18:12.710 --> 18:16.150
By all means! I'd be happy to!

18:16.450 --> 18:17.540
Thank you.

18:20.350 --> 18:22.190
Okay, see you at the clubroom.

18:22.290 --> 18:23.310
Okay.

18:24.690 --> 18:26.220
Yes! Yes!

18:26.730 --> 18:29.790
Yes! Yes! Yes!

18:30.160 --> 18:31.760
Yes!

18:34.940 --> 18:37.900
Yeah, they've made
a provisional decision.

18:38.010 --> 18:40.470
That's awesome! Congratulations!

18:40.570 --> 18:42.630
Hey, you did it. Congrats.

18:43.210 --> 18:46.910
Heh, thanks. For everything.

18:47.150 --> 18:48.580
Everything, huh?

18:49.580 --> 18:50.710
C-Congr...

18:50.820 --> 18:51.790
Where?

18:51.890 --> 18:54.820
It's called Washidasha
Editorial Production.

18:54.920 --> 18:56.020
A subcontractor?

18:56.020 --> 18:57.150
A subcontractor?
Yeah.

18:57.260 --> 19:00.420
But it's actual editorial
work with manga artists.

19:01.600 --> 19:02.800
That was your original aim.

19:02.800 --> 19:04.960
That was your original aim.
After a kick in the butt.

19:05.070 --> 19:06.190
Sorry.

19:06.930 --> 19:10.270
I wondered if maybe
I went too far, but that beard...

19:10.370 --> 19:12.340
It's shaved and gone.

19:14.170 --> 19:15.660
Oh, hey, Ohno.

19:16.240 --> 19:19.240
Did you already send
those dojinshi to America?

19:19.710 --> 19:22.440
Yes, I did. Just the other day.

19:22.550 --> 19:26.690
Okay. Then whenever
a good chance comes up...

19:26.690 --> 19:29.090
Irohagokko
...could you send this to Sue and Angela?

19:29.390 --> 19:32.790
Sure, that's fine, but are you sure?

19:33.090 --> 19:35.890
Yup. I got permission from Kugayama.

19:36.000 --> 19:38.590
Oh, you got in touch with him?

19:39.530 --> 19:41.630
How's Kugapee doing?

19:41.740 --> 19:44.030
It seems he's drawing again.

19:44.140 --> 19:46.070
That's not what I meant.

19:47.010 --> 19:48.940
He said he's making his way.

19:49.040 --> 19:51.510
Gotcha. That's sales for you.

19:52.810 --> 19:54.840
What's up, Ogiue? You're quiet.

19:56.280 --> 19:58.580
N-Not especially.

19:59.020 --> 20:00.110
What gives?

20:00.420 --> 20:02.620
I'm not sure I trust that reaction.

20:03.020 --> 20:06.250
Well, I mean... congratulations.

20:06.530 --> 20:08.430
Thank you for your help.

20:11.470 --> 20:14.060
Saki told me about it. Congrats.

20:14.170 --> 20:16.140
Ohno told me about it. Congrats.

20:16.240 --> 20:19.930
Way to go! I just
heard it from both of them...

20:20.540 --> 20:22.900
Progress Chart
Chiba
Shimizu
Yamashita
Tama
Kohsaka

20:28.550 --> 20:31.920
Toyotamakita General Hospital

20:31.920 --> 20:34.680
We were so into talking...

20:34.820 --> 20:41.490
...about trivial stuff that the final
chime snuck up on us and rang.

20:42.130 --> 20:47.670
So we pass by the lecture cancellation
board and part at the monorail.

20:47.670 --> 20:50.570
So we pass by the lecture cancellation
board and part at the monorail.
Kohsaka, how goes
the game company?

20:50.570 --> 20:52.810
So we pass by the lecture cancellation
board and part at the monorail.
Are you busy? I hear it's pretty rough.

20:52.810 --> 20:53.700
Are you busy? I hear it's pretty rough.

20:53.810 --> 20:54.840
That's not true.
Not as much as I thought.

20:54.840 --> 20:56.810
